### 4. Cloud Service Delivery, Deployment Models, and Infrastructure Abstraction

#### Context & Strategic Importance

Adopting cloud computing shifts threat boundaries from physical server perimeters to software-defined hypervisors and identity boundaries. Cloud infrastructure operates under a shared responsibility model, where security operations tasks are divided between the Cloud Service Provider (CSP) and the customer based on the selected service delivery model.

#### Cloud Service Models & Shared Responsibility

Cloud resources are delivered across three core primary service models—Software as a Service (SaaS), Platform as a Service (PaaS), and Infrastructure as a Service (IaaS)—supplemented by specialized frameworks such as Security as a Service (SECaaS).

